[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue. It is not one issue, so each problem has its
own ticket. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser is fixed and the hint will not be
fixed, because the booking-v3 form is retired. The update says nothing about the one-day moves.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="https://github.com/petestewart/mega-s01e03-support-kb" />

<Callout kind="warn">
The one-day moves are still open. #4471 is closed, but a day/month fix does not explain a one-day
shift. If a report like these comes in after 5 October, add it to ticket 3 and do not merge it
into a closed ticket.
</Callout>

## The problems

**Parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. A tenant that writes the day first
gets day and month swapped, through any channel. Every tenant on file writes the day first.

**Hint.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what it tells them, and
the form reads the date the tenant's way. This happens only on the form channel of booking-v3
tenants. Their app and email reports are parser reports.

**One-day moves.** These reports show a date one day off, or a different day for two people looking
at the same meeting. A swap of day and month cannot do that. The cause is not proven: time zone
conversion is the first thing to check, and the export holds no data that confirms it.

## How to place a report

Go by the tenant and the channel, as `causes.ts` does. Do not use the intake tag: it follows the
reporter's browser, so it marks day-first tenants on `en-US` browsers as `hint`. Do not use the
subject line either, because the same subject appears on reports with different causes (see
[triage](/kb/triage/dedupe)).

